{"title":"Career Roadmap: Dealer","role":"Dealer","summary":"A Dealer executes buy and sell orders for financial products on behalf of clients or an institution, depending on the organization and authorization involved. The role can cover:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"Financial Markets (BFM) / Banking & Insurance (BBI)"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build financial-market knowledge, market analysis, trading systems, risk management, compliance and execution skills"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Dealer executes buy and sell orders for financial products on behalf of clients or an institution, depending on the organization and authorization involved. The role can cover:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equities"},{"text":"Bonds"},{"text":"Derivatives"},{"text":"Currency products"},{"text":"Commodities"},{"text":"Mutual-fund/market products in relevant distribution settings"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A dealer needs strong knowledge of capital markets, order execution, market microstructure, technical and fundamental analysis, risk controls, trading technology and regulatory compliance."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"In India, dealing and trading activities can involve regulated entities, exchange memberships, intermediary registrations and role-specific certification/authorization requirements. A B.Com degree alone does not automatically authorize a person to execute regulated transactions independently."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Finance & economics foundation"},{"text":"Accounting, economics, statistics"},{"text":"Market-analysis assignments"},{"text":"Weak quantitative foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Capital-market knowledge"},{"text":"Equity, debt, derivatives, exchanges"},{"text":"Paper-trading journal"},{"text":"Treating trading as gambling"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Execution & risk management"},{"text":"Market microstructure, technical analysis, compliance"},{"text":"Trading simulation + analytics"},{"text":"Ignoring risk and regulations"}],[{"text":"Final Stage"},{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"Terminals, Excel, Python, certification preparation"},{"text":"Internship + market portfolio"},{"text":"No practical market exposure"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial Accounting"},{"text":"Business Economics"},{"text":"Business Mathematics"},{"text":"Business Communication"},{"text":"Introduction to Financial Markets"},{"text":"Excel fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Corporate Finance"},{"text":"Banking fundamentals"},{"text":"Financial instruments"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Financial statement analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equity Markets"},{"text":"Debt Markets"},{"text":"Stock exchanges"},{"text":"Market participants"},{"text":"Order types"},{"text":"Trading terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Derivatives"},{"text":"Futures"},{"text":"Options"},{"text":"Foreign exchange"},{"text":"Commodities"},{"text":"Market microstructure"},{"text":"Trading systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technical analysis"},{"text":"Fundamental analysis"},{"text":"Risk management"},{"text":"Portfolio concepts"},{"text":"Trading psychology"},{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"Market surveillance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Algorithmic trading fundamentals"},{"text":"Python for finance"},{"text":"Financial analytics"},{"t